#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# symmetry_commutator

#% text
# `symmetry_commutator(v, w, vars)` gives the commutator `[v, w]` of the vector fields `v = sum v_i d/dvars_i` and `w`, given by their lists of components over the variables `vars`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The components of `[v, w]` are `sum_j (v_j d(w_i, vars_j) - w_j d(v_i, vars_j))`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The translation and the projective generator of sl(2):

#% cell
symmetry_commutator([1, 0], [x^2, x*y], [x, y])
#% output
#= [2*x, y]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The commutator is antisymmetric:

#% cell
symmetry_commutator([x, 0], [y, x], [x, y]) + symmetry_commutator([y, x], [x, 0], [x, y])
#% output
#= [0, 0]

